    "oracle": "Official cached Maven Spark4.2.1, Comet disabled, same inputs and ANSI=true; compare values, duplicates, schema and required error classes/SQLSTATE."
  },
  "implementation": {
    "J05": "Lower ScalarSubquery leaves to typed runtime arguments; refresh scalar/vector masks every batch, including nested getters and null fast paths; reject malformed cardinality before unsafe loads. Current dispatcher digest/occurrence architecture retained.",
    "J06": "Retain deterministic eager-safe-prefix CASE masks and balanced AND segments. Keep actual Spark whole-stage eligibility, top-level Filter NULL policy, inferred null-check/CSE ordering and optional-off correctness separate from expression three-valued logic.",
    "J07": "Compact typed function refs and live driver-captured task payloads; Spark serializes shared object graphs once per task-binary stream and afresh per action. JDK weak identity registry, strict task-only lookup, completion/retry/cancellation guards, no Guava pool cache. Include late prepared scan commons, opaque Delta and every runtime root.",
    "J17": "Keep heavy native shuffle spec on map-side RDD/iterator, transient on dependency; retain small SQLConf for executor admission and fallback. Make operator protobuf/serialized-plan caches transient while explicit execution carriers retain required plans. Intern SQL text in scans, Delta envelopes and shuffle roots without changing source keys or error positions.",
    "C02": "Exact lazy native AND/OR masks, NULL evaluation, dual-fallible/stateful row ordering, projected RHS columns, validated compact lengths before scatter, and safe missing-child errors. Guard operator-wide unsafe CSE; retain one JVM occurrence for stateful COALESCE/multiple IF/CASE occurrences and honor child config/maxFields guards. Concrete known string functions retain the upstream vector kernel with physical-type/scalar bounds proofs."
  },
